    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting the soft matchup against G. Holmes, making **Bryce Harper** (76.78) and **Luis Arraez** (68.31) our primary offensive anchors. The standout play of the day, however, is **Cal Raleigh** (78.02). Facing Jacob Lopez, **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a massive 19% bump due to the SP's struggles and a favorable park factor, positioning him as the highest-ceiling start in the lineup despite the \"Lineup Pending\" designation. **Lawrence Butler** (69.23) also earns a premium spot today; his dynamic platoon advantage against Bryce Miller, combined with a 10% park boost, makes him a high-efficiency weapon as we hunt for counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved the final utility spot, where **Yainer Diaz** (54.72) narrowly edged out **Dylan Beavers** (49.94) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.39). While **Dylan Beavers** boasts the advantage of a leadoff spot, the sheer difficulty of facing Dylan Cease forced him to the bench in favor of **Yainer Diaz**, whose base projection remains more resilient despite a tougher venue. We are also keeping a close eye on **Alex Freeland** (44.16), whose score is suppressed significantly by the #9 spot in the order; should the actual lineup shift him higher, his value against Eury P\u00e9rez could spike, though he remains a marginal play for now.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Zack Gelof**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Yainer Diaz**. While we anticipate these players will hold their assumed spots, any defensive adjustments or late scratches could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Tyler Freeman** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom remain unavailable, but for today, the focus is purely on capitalizing on the identified platoon edges to keep our Roto standing afloat in this late-season push.",
